      "title": "Select-all overwrites range anchor even if rejected",
      "message": "Select-all is dispatched as ListSelectionEvent with only IDs set and TargetID set to the focused row. If Apply interprets the event using TargetID, modifiers or anchor (range/toggle semantics), the result may differ from \"all enabled rows\". It also overwrites listAnchor before the application accepts or rejects the proposal, so a rejected select-all still moves the range anchor and changes later Shift-range behavior.",
